 36S  c  J|p=3/2+ for {+37}Cl ground state (2012Ca15).                          
 36S  c  1970Gr02: E(d)=28.9 MeV deuterons from the University of Michigan      
 36S 2c  83-inch cyclotron. Target was 90-|mg/cm{+2} NaCl enriched to 99.3% in  
 36S 3c  {+37}Cl, vacuum-evaporated onto thin carbon backings; overall target   
 36S 4c  normalization uncertainty 15% from |a-particle energy loss and elastic 
 36S 5c  deuteron scattering. Recoiling {+3}He ions were detected with a counter
 36S 6c  telescope (|DE=100 |mm, E=500 |mm, FWHM=110 keV) for |q|>12|' and with 
 36S 7c  a three-stage magnetic spectrograph (FWHM=25 keV) using Ilford K0      
 36S 8c  nuclear emulsion plates behind Al absorbers; a position-sensitive      
 36S 9c  detector (14|*50 mm, 240 |mm depletion depth) was used at extreme      
 36S Ac  forward angles |q|>2.5|'. Measured Q-values, {+3}He spectra, |s(|q)    
 36S Bc  from 2.5|' to 60|', and elastic deuteron scattering for beam           
 36S Cc  normalization. Deduced levels up to E=7.71 MeV, L-transfers, J|p and   
 36S Dc  C{+2}S. DWBA analysis with the code DWUCK using non-local finite-range 
 36S Ec  corrections; shell-model calculations for four proton holes in the     
 36S Fc  2s-1d shell in SU(3) and j-j coupling. States at 2.00, 2.89 and 3.36   
 36S Gc  MeV reported in (t,p) work are not observed; upper limits are set on   
 36S Hc  their C{+2}S. The 4.52-4.58 MeV doublet unresolved in earlier          
 36S Ic  (d,{+3}He) work is resolved here, and the 6.511 level is identified    
 36S Jc  with the level reported at 6.60 MeV. See also 1968Gr04 from the same   
 36S Kc  group.                                                                 
